@crew walsh-esme
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hello. Walsh, galley. Trays are on the left. Mind the wet patch.
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Your collar's folded. Other side.
- {hi}. Soup's at ninety degrees. Give it two minutes.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I kept you a bread roll. The good end.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good shift. Every carrot the same size. Nobody noticed. I noticed.   #funny
? mood:low
- Long one. Cleaned the clean pans twice. Brennan saw. Said nothing.

== near
? act:work
- Hold the knife like this. Thumb back. There. Now it does the work.
? act:gym
- Promenade, then the treadmill. Same pace as yesterday. To the second.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- My fish are back home on Port Halloran. My brother feeds them. Badly, I expect.
? tier>=colleague
- Gerald's on my windowsill. Every cactus aboard is Gerald. Mine's the tidiest one.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Laps of the promenade before shift. Eight of them. Nobody talks to you on lap six.

== about
? bond:best
- {best} runs with me. Same pace, no talking. Perfect.   #warm

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning. You're early. Good. Early's the only time worth being anywhere.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}. Late team's on. Dinner's ninety degrees and falling. Go now.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- You're back. You've missed four soups. I counted.   #funny

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- {bye}. Mind your elbows in the queue.
? tier>=friend
- Thanks. That was a good talk. I don't say that much.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Fine. Steady. Everything where it should be.

== near
? act:dinner
- Tray straight, please. It's not a rule. It should be.
? deck:3 time:morning
- Lap six. Don't talk to me on lap six. Lap seven's fine.   #funny

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Brennan says I'm the only one who can dice like she does. I wrote it down.
? tier>=friend
- I stay late too often. I know. Someone has to finish the clean-down. Someone always is me.

== invite
? trad:running tier>=acquaintance
- Running club. Come along. I don't talk while I run. You'll like it.

== accept
- Yes. I'll be there. On time.
== decline
- No. Sorry. Clean-down. Another time.
== missed
- You didn't come. I waited eight minutes. Then I left. That's my rule.
== birthday
? birthday:me
- My birthday. I've told nobody. Now I've told you. Don't make it a thing.   #funny
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I made you something small. It's perfectly square.   #warm
== hint
- Got a minute? A quiet one.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Forty grams. Not forty-two.
- Someone chopped these big. Ivo.   #funny
- Hm. Soup's two minutes off.
- Same pace as yesterday. To the second.
? act:work
- Lids on. Labels out.

== rumour
- I don't repeat things. This once.
- Heard it at the pass. Usually true.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- You brought it. On time. Correct weight. Thank you.   #warm
? told:fav.job
- You did my job. Properly. I checked. It was proper.   #warm
? told:fixed.range
- The range holds its heat now. Steady. Was that you? Good.
? told:fixed.extractor
- Extractor's pulling clean. Steam goes where it should. Thank you.
? told:came.running
- You ran with us. Your pace was even. That's rare.   #warm
? told:gift.book
- I read your book. In order. Twice. It was good. That's all.   #warm
? told:bday
- You noticed my birthday. Hm. Thank you. That was nice.   #warm

// Writer 3, batch 6: your standing with their department (rep:, "this band or better") and what you're known for
// (you:), as greet lines (the head writer: the rep and knownFor kinds wait until the game calls them).

== greet
? rep:well tier>=acquaintance
- Galley thinks you're tidy. I agree. That's two.
? rep:theirs
- You're on the galley list now. The good list. Short list.   #warm
? you:reliable
- You're known for turning up on time. So am I. Good company.

// Writer 3, batch 8: thanks for a gift (gift: loved | liked | polite, or the gift's tag; dialogue 0.43.10).

== gift
? gift:loved
- That's exactly right. Thank you. I'll keep it on the shelf. Square to the edge.   #warm
? gift:liked
- Thank you. Useful. I like useful.
? gift:polite
- Hm. Thank you. I'll find the right place for it.

// Writer 3, batch 9: asking after your people back home (the home flags; only the big news you'd have told them).

== greet
? flag:home.gran.won tier>=colleague
- A prize marrow. What did it weigh? Your gran will know to the gram. Ask her.

// Writer 4, batch 2: everyday chatter, not about work (meals, rest days, home, hobbies, seasons, traditions).
== smalltalk
? act:meal
- This is the good jam. Don't tell Ivo.   #funny
- Soup, bread, a pear. That's a meal.
- Seconds? One ladle. Not a big ladle.   #funny
? act:breakfast
- Toast. Two minutes a side. Then it's toast.
? act:off
- Rest day. Laps, then a book. Then laps.
- Wrote to my brother. One page. Enough.
- Fed Gerald. One drop. He's a cactus.   #funny
? time:evening
- My brother says the fish are fat. Too fat.   #funny
- Forty laps. Same pace. Good.
? time:morning
- Up at five. The laps are quiet then.
? season:lanterns
- My lantern's square. It's tidier.   #funny
? season:sowing
- Planted mine in a straight line. Obviously.   #funny
? trad:quiz
- Quiz tonight. I'll take the numbers ones.
? time:night
- Rain on Port Halloran sounds like frying. I miss it.

== rumour
- Ivo told me. So it was long. Short version: yes.   #funny
- I heard one thing. I'll say it once.

// Writer 4, batch 7: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. Forty minutes. Labelled boxes. Obviously.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- I'm off to a new ship. Keep the carrots even for me.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- I don't say much. So: you were good company. Thank you. That's the useful part.   #warm

== letter
- New galley. They cut the onions too big. I've said nothing. Yet. The fish are well, my brother says.
? tier>=friend
- Ran my laps this morning and counted the Wren's corridors in my head. Forty. Still the right number. Hello to you.
